        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "054abe95-97fa-57c7-b8d2-878b7765e2a2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Bruce Geller, Richard Levinson, William Link, Gail Fisher, Joe Mannix, Peggy Fair\n- Works: Mannix, Please Don't Eat the Babies\n- Roles: private investigator, secretary\n- Awards: Golden Globe Awards, Emmy Award\n\nFacts:\n- Bruce Geller was born on October 13, 1930, and he was an American lyricist, screenwriter, director, and television producer.\n- In 1968, Gail Fisher began playing secretary Peggy Fair on the television detective series Mannix.\n- Mannix was created by Richard Levinson and William Link, and Bruce Geller developed the series as executive producer.\n- In Mannix, the title character Joe Mannix is a private investigator.\n- From 1968 through 1975, Gail Fisher played Peggy Fair on Mannix and won two Golden Globe Awards and an Emmy Award for the role.\n- Gail Fisher was the first black woman to win either a Golden Globe Award or an Emmy Award.\n- Bruce Geller directed the 1983 American horror thriller film Please Don't Eat the Babies, which was also known as Island Fury.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
